  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A spring of negligible mass has a length of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span> cm. When the spring is extended to a length of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"32\"></span> cm, the energy stored in the spring is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"36\"></span> J. The tension in the spring is proportional to the extension of the spring. What is the work done by the spring when its length changes from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"32\"></span> cm to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"24\"></span> cm?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.0\"></span> J</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"12\"></span> J</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"24\"></span> J</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"32\"></span> J</li>\n</ol>"
